  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 3e4b5683c1ea36345958694d590b6436, type: 3}
  m_Name: COC3_Quiz_LO3_Testing_Q02
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::QuizQuestionData
  questionText: Why write the test plan BEFORE doing any testing?
  choices:
  - It is required by the software
  - It is faster than testing as you go
  - So nothing is skipped and the pass criteria are not decided after the fact
  - So the client can be billed for it separately
  correctChoiceIndex: 2
  points: 10
  explanation: A plan written afterwards is a description of what happened to work.
    Written first, it is a standard the work has to meet.
